{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+, Antioxidant", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "CD", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals this sequence is most similar (55%) to Brevinin-1SPb. Activity: Active only against the tested Gram+ bacteria, including S. aureus ATCC25923 (MIC 4.68 ug/mL), S. aureus 090223+ (IS) and N. asteroids 090312+ (IS) (MIC 37.5 ug/mL). SAR: Without C-terminal amidation (with S-S bond), the peptide lost activity. Without the Rana box (with amidation), the peptide became less active (MIC 37.5-75 ug/mL). Structure: However, all the peptide analogs remain helical in 50% TFE water solution. In vitro Toxicity: Little hemolysis at 100 ug/mL. Hemolysis of human RBC increased without C-terminal amidation (15.4%), Rana box (17.9%), or both (20.8%).", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "30127331", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Zool Res. 2019 May 18;40(3):198-204. doi: 10.24272/j.issn.2095-8137.2018.070. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03218", "source_id": "AP03218", "source_numeric_id": "03218", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03218", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Effects of C-terminal amidation and heptapeptide ring on the biological activities and advanced structure of amurin-9KY, a novel antimicrobial peptide identified from the brown frog, Rana kunyuensis", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
